# LearnLoop — environment variables

Copy to `.env.local` for development. Never commit secrets.

```bash
# --- Database (pooled for serverless) ---
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/learnloop?pgbouncer=true"
# Direct URL for migrations (Neon/Supabase often provide both)
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/learnloop"

# --- Clerk ---
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="pk_test_..."
CLERK_SECRET_KEY="sk_test_..."
CLERK_WEBHOOK_SECRET="whsec_..."

# --- OpenAI (optional until AI routes enabled) ---
OPENAI_API_KEY="sk-..."

# --- Realtime (optional until socket host deployed) ---
# Browser + Next use SOCKET_SERVER_URL; socket script listens on SOCKET_PORT (default 3001).
SOCKET_SERVER_URL="http://127.0.0.1:3001"
SOCKET_JWT_SECRET="min-32-chars-random-socket-jwt"
# Next server calls the socket process to push invalidations (same machine in dev):
SOCKET_SERVER_INTERNAL_URL="http://127.0.0.1:3001"
SOCKET_INTERNAL_SECRET="min-32-chars-internal-publish"
# SOCKET_PORT=3001
# SOCKET_CORS_ORIGINS="http://localhost:3000,http://127.0.0.1:3000"
# Dev: private LAN origins (192.168.x.x, 10.x.x, 172.16–31.x) are allowed unless SOCKET_CORS_STRICT=1.
# SOCKET_CORS_STRICT=1
# Other devices on Wi‑Fi: set SOCKET_SERVER_URL to this host’s LAN IP (not 127.0.0.1), e.g. http://192.168.1.10:3001
# In `next dev`, learner session fee on rating is skipped unless LEARNLOOP_CHARGE_SESSION_FEE=1 (production charges; NEXT_PUBLIC_LEARNLOOP_DEMO=1 also skips the fee).
# LEARNLOOP_CHARGE_SESSION_FEE=1
# Run Next + socket sidecar: `npm run dev:realtime`

# --- Redis / rate limits (optional) ---
REDIS_URL="redis://default:pass@host:6379"

# --- AI jobs (optional; verify on ingress) ---
AI_QUEUE_SECRET="..."
```

**Vercel:** Production + Preview envs; use separate databases for preview to protect prod data.

## Demo Day (optional)

```bash
# Client: faster polling + BroadcastChannel heartbeat for “alive” dashboards
NEXT_PUBLIC_LEARNLOOP_DEMO=1

# Seed: wipe + insert ~56 demo users, 100+ open doubts, sessions, leaderboard (same shell)
DEMO_ECOSYSTEM_SEED=1 npm run db:seed:demo
```

`NEXT_PUBLIC_LEARNLOOP_DEMO=1` also enables softer server fallbacks when the DB hiccups during a live pitch.
